<title>CHILE: Exxon Chile smelter maintenance finished.</title>
<headline>Exxon Chile smelter maintenance finished.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maintenance work at Exxon Mineral's Chagres smelter in Chile has finished and output will restart within the next fiveto-seven days, said an official at Minera Disputada de las Condes, which operates the plant.</p>
<p>&quot;The work carried out while the smelter was closed in August and September has been completed as programmed,&quot; spokesman Guillermo Garcia told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;The plant has started reheating and hopes to begin smelting within the next five to seven days.&quot;</p>
</text>
